  "_meta": {
    "purpose": "Structured, interactive version of the New York Times 'Population Control, Marauder Style' data-graphic (Bill Marsh, NYT, 6 Nov 2011), which itself renders the death-toll estimates catalogued by Matthew White in 'The Great Big Book of Horrible Things' (W. W. Norton, 2011). Each event carries an estimated death toll, its span, category, and location so the atlas can plot the scale of human loss over time and by region.",
    "honesty": "These are ESTIMATES from a single popular-history compilation. White himself stresses that pre-modern tolls are guesses drawn from a spread of historians, often with wide error bars. Figures are 'deaths in millions' as printed in the NYT graphic. We reproduce them faithfully and label the source; we do NOT present them as settled fact. Where a figure is especially contested, contested=true and a note explains why. India-relevant events are tagged india_region so the heritage atlas can link a temple's destruction to its regional toll.",
